'''''Euphorbia horrida''''', the '''African milk barrel''', or '''horrid spurge,''' is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] Euphorbiaceae, [[native plant|native]] to South Africa. It is a cactus-like [[shrub]] showing remarkable similarities to the true [[cactus|cacti]] of the New World, and thus an example of [[convergent evolution]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Cactus art - ''Euphorbia horrida''|url=http://www.cactus-art.biz/schede/EUPHORBIA/Euphorbia_horrida/Euphorbia_horrida/Euphorbia_horrida.htm|access-date=19 June 2013}}</ref> Growing to {{convert|1.5|m|0|abbr=on}}, it has blue-green, heavily ridged spiny stems carrying solitary green flowers in summer. In [[temperateness|temperate]] regions it must be grown in heated conditions under glass, or as a houseplant on a sunny windowsill.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Euphorbia horrida (African Milk Barrel) |url=https://www.gardenia.net/plant/euphorbia-horrida-african-milk-barrel-grow-care-guide |access-date=2026-01-06 |website=Gardenia |language=en-US}}</ref>

== Range and habitat ==
''Euphorbia horrida'' is found in arid deserts in the southeastern cape of Africa.<ref>{{Cite web |title=African milk barrel (Euphorbia horrida) |url=https://www.inaturalist.org/taxa/521486-Euphorbia-horrida |access-date=2026-02-02 |website=iNaturalist |language=en}}</ref> It is found in sandy, gravely soils that remain dry for most of the year. When it does rain, ''Euphorbia horrida'' rapidly absorbs water, expanding the ribs and swelling into a rotund, cylindrical shape. <ref>{{Cite web |title=Euphorbia horrida |url=https://diameterplants.com/products/euphorbia-horrida |access-date=2026-02-02 |website=Diameter Plants |language=en}}</ref>

== Toxicity. ==
When damaged, ''Euphorbia horrida'' rapidly releases a white sap, like of most plants in the ''Euphorbia'' genus''.'' The sap is toxic, and causes eye and skin irritation. Left to dry, the sap becomes a sticky, clear, and hard-to-remove resin that remains toxic. <ref>{{Cite web |last=MD |first=Thomas Osborne |date=2013-04-24 |title=Euphorbia: A dangerous ally |url=https://tastylandscape.com/2013/04/24/122/ |access-date=2026-02-02 |website=TastyLandscape |language=en-US}}</ref>

